WHAT: Raises max_multi_use_inlinee_blocks from 4 to 8 and insts from
16 to 24 in speed mode. Allows larger multi-use helper functions to
be inlined.

WHY: ABI decoder helpers with 3-4 blocks (error check branches) were
still blocked by the previous limit of 4. Raising to 8 lets these
larger helpers get inlined.

GAS IMPACT: -222 gas total.
  governance/delegate: -74
  governance/propose: -74
  governance/vote: -74

CODEGEN IMPACT: Only governance benefited. The delegate/propose/vote
functions have ABI decode helpers just over the previous size limit.

TEAM NOTES: Third inliner tuning commit (steps 3, 4, 11). Total from
all three: ~1100 gas, exclusively on governance. This is the ceiling
for inliner parameter tuning — the stubborn contracts need source-level
changes (Fe std library) not optimizer knob-turning.
